; The child of the insecure delegation.  It signs its data anyway, and
; clove is told to put another zone's name in the signer field, so that
; no key a resolver can reach will verify what this zone sends.
;
; That is insecure.mufj.jp of 2020: its answers carried an RRSIG whose
; signer said "sharp", a zone which had not signed them, under a
; delegation from mufj.jp which carried no DS.
$ORIGIN insecure.example.
$TTL 3600
@	IN	SOA	ns.insecure.example. root.example. 1 3600 900 604800 3600
@	IN	NS	ns.insecure.example.
ns	IN	{{AUTH_ADDR_RR}}
host	IN	A	192.0.2.9
